LoongOffice Debian source inputs
================================

The package is intentionally built without network access. debian/rules never
clones a repository and does not build the proprietary OFD extension from
source.

Connected preparation checkout
------------------------------

On a connected, trusted preparation host, build the Gerrit submission input
with one command:

    debian/scripts/prepare-orig-tarball

Run it from a clean Git checkout of the LoongOffice release branch, with
dpkg-dev, Git, curl or wget, and the normal LibreOffice build prerequisites
installed.

It fetches the exact source commits, downloads and verifies LibreOffice's
external tarballs, and writes ../loongoffice_<upstream-version>.orig.tar.xz.
Submit that orig tarball together with the debian/ directory to the
system-source Gerrit project. This replaces dh_make --createorig: the output
contains the required submodules, batch-print source, and offline LibreOffice
tarballs, but not private OFD or OFDRW source.

The preparation script runs the following source fetch step itself. It can also
be run independently when refreshing only the Git inputs:

    debian/scripts/fetch-vendor-sources

The repository URLs and expected commits are recorded in
debian/vendor-sources.lock and checked at the start of every build. The script
also initializes the dictionaries, helpcontent2, and translations submodules
required by the configured LibreOffice build. Their lock entries must match the
gitlinks in the main repository.

The custom vendor directories are deliberately not Git submodules:
LibreOffice's pre-commit hook rejects gitlink changes, and gitlinks alone are
unusable in an isolated CI. Updating a source therefore requires an intentional
lock-file update.

Proprietary OFD input
---------------------

The private OFD and OFDRW sources must never be included in the exported
vendor archive or a public source package. A trusted internal builder uses a
separate private checkout to produce loongoffice-ofd-extension.oxt and imports
only that artifact:

    debian/scripts/import-ofd-oxt /path/to/loongoffice-ofd-extension.oxt

This writes debian/prebuilt/loongoffice-ofd-extension.oxt and its SHA256 file.
The OXT is explicitly listed in debian/source/include-binaries and the text
checksum is included with the other debian/ files, so an upstream builder can
create the complete binary package without access to OFD source. debian/rules
validates the digest and rejects OXT archives containing common
implementation-source file types before the LibreOffice build starts.
debian/source/options also excludes any private OFD, OFDRW, and Maven working
directories left on a trusted release host. This is defence in depth; do not
add those directories to Git or an uploaded vendor archive.

LibreOffice external tarballs
-----------------------------

LibreOffice also builds configuration-selected third-party projects. On the
connected target platform, download the complete set with LibreOffice's own
download rules:

    debian/scripts/prepare-libreoffice-tarballs

The connected preparation host needs curl (preferred) or wget. The script
rejects a missing download client before configuring or changing the tarball
input.

The script configures with the same flags as debian/rules, downloads into
vendor/libreoffice-tarballs, and records the configuration, platform, build
type, file list, and SHA256 checksums. Package builds keep automatic fetching
disabled and reject a missing, changed, or incompatible tarball input.

CI without access to GitHub
---------------------------

The orig tarball made by prepare-orig-tarball already contains all Git and
tarball inputs required by the offline build. The OFD OXT is carried by the
debian/ directory, rather than by the orig tarball. The older
export-vendor-sources helper remains available only for environments that
manage the vendor archive independently.

Build layout
------------

LibreOffice is installed directly with:

    DESTDIR=debian/loongoffice make distro-pack-install

The application lives below /opt/loongoffice while desktop integration and
launchers use /usr. Packaging removes the generic libreoffice, soffice, and
component wrappers created by distro-pack-install, leaving only branded
LoongOffice entry points. This allows the distribution LibreOffice packages to
remain installed without shared command paths. The generated bootstraprc must
also use the independent $SYSUSERCONFIG/loongoffice/4 profile. Bash completion
and AppStream component IDs are rewritten to LoongOffice-only names rather than
registering or replacing their LibreOffice equivalents.

The distribution installer reads generated desktop inputs from the configured
INSTALLDIRNAME path, currently workdir/CustomTarget/sysui/share/loongoffice.
It fails before packaging if MIME, desktop, or template inputs are incomplete.

The OFD OXT is unpacked as a bundled extension. Batch print is installed as
Python source and uses the system Python selected explicitly for PyUNO, plus
distribution-provided PySide6, PyMuPDF, CUPS, libmagic, and lru-dict modules.
Its packaged executable lookup never falls back to /usr/lib/libreoffice. No
intermediate DEB is generated or unpacked.

The Loongnix dwz implementation cannot process the full private ELF set below
/opt/loongoffice. Packaging therefore skips dh_dwz, which is only an optional
DWARF deduplication optimization; normal stripping and dependency generation
remain enabled.
